/-!
# Mathieu branches of the sporadic FF-normalizer exclusion

The M11 branch is proved for arbitrary finite quasisimple covers, with a
faithful irreducible binary action and its literal full linear normalizer.
The M12, M22 (including odd covers), and M23/M24 branches remain independent
representation obligations. This module does not assert their exclusions.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, B.1.13,
printed pp.73–74, citing Guralnick–Malle, *Classification of 2F-modules, II*,
Table 2, DOI 10.1515/9783110198126.117.
-/
